{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/ast_index.cljc | sed -n '1,205p'; nl -ba test/yin/repl/ast_index_test.cljc | sed -n '225,355p'; git diff -- src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc; cat collab/1790742782000-vm-engineer-repl-ast-index-slice1.claude-opus-5-5.report-r4.md\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yin.repl.ast-index\n     2\t  \"The shell's AST indexer: the `$ast` row relation and the `$occ`\n     3\t   occurrence relation over every program the session expanded\n     4\t   (collab/1790708845000-architect-repl-ast-row-relation, §1-2).\n     5\t\n     6\t   It is a peer observer on `program-out`, attached beside the evaluator's\n     7\t   and `yin.repl.index`'s and advanced by the evaluation round: the three\n     8\t   share only the medium, and none reads another.  Each forwarded tree\n     9\t   packet `[root rows]` adds its canonical rows to `:rows`, keyed by node\n    10\t   address — one row per distinct address, so `$ast` is its values — and\n    11\t   its `[root path node]` places, derived by `yin.vm/occurrences`, to\n    12\t   `:occurrences` — one tuple per distinct place.  An identical root or\n    13\t   row observed again multiplies neither relation.\n    14\t\n    15\t   Both relations are in-memory session projections: rebuildable from the\n    16\t   medium, published nowhere, carrying no origin or clock slot, and the\n    17\t   same under the `:current` and `:history` views, since observed code is\n    18\t   only ever added.  Reset and VM selection rebuild them with the session.\n    19\t\n    20\t   Loss is reported, never hidden, and never stops the evaluator: a gap is\n    21\t   counted on the observer (`:ingress-gaps`) and marks the indexer\n    22\t   `:lost?`; a malformed packet, a row whose address is not the content\n    23\t   address of its body, a row that differs (metadata included) from the\n    24\t   one already held at its address, or a failed derivation is recorded\n    25\t   under `:failure`.\n    26\t   Either leaves the relations unavailable (`relations` answers nil) —\n    27\t   never a partial snapshot — and later packets are consumed without being\n    28\t   indexed until the session is rebuilt.  A packet is merged only once it\n    29\t   is wholly derived.\"\n    30\t  (:require [dao.jing :as jing]\n    31\t            [dao.stream.observer :as observer]\n    32\t            [yin.vm :as vm]))\n    33\t\n    34\t\n    35\t(defn make-indexer\n    36\t  \"The AST indexer for one session over `observer`, attached to\n    37\t   `program-out` beside the evaluator's.\"\n    38\t  [{:keys [observer]}]\n    39\t  {:observer observer\n    40\t   :rows {}\n    41\t   :occurrences #{}\n    42\t   :programs 0\n    43\t   :lost? false\n    44\t   :failure nil})\n    45\t\n    46\t\n    47\t(defn- same-value?\n    48\t  \"`=` that also compares metadata at every depth, as `yin.vm.macro`'s\n    49\t   packet validator does: the canonical encoding strips reader positions,\n    50\t   so two bodies may share an address while differing there.\"\n    51\t  [a b]\n    52\t  (and (= a b)\n    53\t       (= (meta a) (meta b))\n    54\t       (or (nil? (meta a)) (same-value? (meta a) (meta b)))\n    55\t       (cond (map? a) (every? (fn [[k v]]\n    56\t                                (let [[k' v'] (find b k)]\n    57\t                                  (and (same-value? k k') (same-value? v v'))))\n    58\t                              a)\n    59\t             (set? a) (every? (fn [e] (same-value? e (some #(when (= e %) %) b)))\n    60\t                              a)\n    61\t             (sequential? a) (every? true? (map same-value? a b))\n    62\t             :else true)))\n    63\t\n    64\t\n    65\t(defn- derive-packet\n    66\t  \"`{:root r :rows {id row} :occurrences #{[root path node]}}` for one\n    67\t   packet, or `{:failure {...}}` when it is malformed or disagrees with\n    68\t   `held`, the rows already indexed.  Every row's address is verified\n    69\t   against its body (`dao.jing/segment-matches?`); a row whose body is `=`\n    70\t   to the held one yet differs in metadata at any depth shares its address\n    71\t   and is refused as `:address-conflict`, never merged over it.\"\n    72\t  [held packet]\n    73\t  (if-not (and (vector? packet)\n    74\t               (= 2 (count packet))\n    75\t               (sequential? (second packet))\n    76\t               (every? #(and (vector? %) (<= 2 (count %))) (second packet)))\n    77\t    {:failure {:stage :packet :reason :shape}}\n    78\t    (let [[root packet-rows] packet\n    79\t          rows (into {} (map (fn [r] [(first r) r])) packet-rows)]\n    80\t      (if (< (count rows) (count packet-rows))\n    81\t        {:failure {:stage :packet :root root :reason :duplicate-address\n    82\t                   :id (some (fn [[id n]] (when (< 1 n) id))\n    83\t                             (frequencies (map first packet-rows)))}}\n    84\t        (if-let [defect (vm/validate-rows {:root root :rows rows})]\n    85\t          {:failure {:stage :packet :root root :reason :invalid-rows\n    86\t                     :defect defect}}\n    87\t          (if-let [forged (some (fn [[id row]]\n    88\t                                  (when-not (jing/segment-matches? id\n    89\t                                                                   (subvec row 1))\n    90\t                                    id))\n    91\t                                rows)]\n    92\t            {:failure {:stage :packet :root root :reason :address-mismatch\n    93\t                       :id forged}}\n    94\t            (if-let [conflict (some (fn [[id row]]\n    95\t                                      (when (and (contains? held id)\n    96\t                                                 (not (same-value? row\n    97\t                                                                   (get held id))))\n    98\t                                        id))\n    99\t                                    rows)]\n   100\t              {:failure {:stage :packet :root root :reason :address-conflict\n   101\t                         :id conflict}}\n   102\t              {:root root\n   103\t               :rows rows\n   104\t               :occurrences (vm/occurrences {:root root :rows rows})})))))))\n   105\t\n   106\t\n   107\t(defn- index-packet\n   108\t  \"Merge one packet's rows and occurrences, or record why it could not be\n   109\t   and leave both relations as they were.\"\n   110\t  [ix packet]\n   111\t  (let [derived (try\n   112\t                  (derive-packet (:rows ix) packet)\n   113\t                  (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) e\n   114\t                    {:failure {:stage :derive :message (ex-message e)}}))]\n   115\t    (if-let [failure (:failure derived)]\n   116\t      (assoc ix :failure failure)\n   117\t      (-> ix\n   118\t          (update :rows into (:rows derived))\n   119\t          (update :occurrences into (:occurrences derived))\n   120\t          (update :programs inc)))))\n   121\t\n   122\t\n   123\t(defn- consume\n   124\t  \"Advance the observer past every packet still on the medium, handing each\n   125\t   to `f` while the indexer is available; a gap marks it lost.\"\n   126\t  [indexer f]\n   127\t  (loop [ix indexer]\n   128\t    (let [{:keys [status batch] observer' :observer}\n   129\t          (observer/observe-next (:observer ix))\n   130\t          ix (assoc ix :observer observer')]\n   131\t      (case status\n   132\t        :ok (recur (if (or (:lost? ix) (:failure ix)) ix (f ix batch)))\n   133\t        :gap (recur (assoc ix :lost? true))\n   134\t        ix))))\n   135\t\n   136\t\n   137\t(defn step\n   138\t  \"The round's AST index step: index every packet `program-out` still\n   139\t   holds for this observer.\"\n   140\t  [indexer]\n   141\t  (consume indexer index-packet))\n   142\t\n   143\t\n   144\t(defn skip\n   145\t  \"Advance the observer past every packet still on the medium without\n   146\t   indexing it: a round that threw before its program ran indexes nothing.\n   147\t   A gap still marks the indexer lost.\"\n   148\t  [indexer]\n   149\t  (consume indexer (fn [ix _packet] ix)))\n   150\t\n   151\t\n   152\t(defn available?\n   153\t  \"Whether the relations are complete for every packet observed.\"\n   154\t  [indexer]\n   155\t  (not (or (:lost? indexer) (:failure indexer))))\n   156\t\n   157\t\n   158\t(defn relations\n   159\t  \"`{:ast [row ...] :occ #{[root path node] ...}}` — the `$ast` rows, one\n   160\t   per distinct address, and the `$occ` tuples — or nil when the indexer\n   161\t   is lost or failed.\"\n   162\t  [indexer]\n   163\t  (when (available? indexer)\n   164\t    {:ast (vec (vals (:rows indexer)))\n   165\t     :occ (:occurrences indexer)}))\n   166\t\n   167\t\n   168\t(defn notice\n   169\t  \"The warning every round must carry while the indexer is unavailable, or\n   170\t   nil when it is healthy: a gap, or the refused packet's `:reason` (a\n   171\t   failed derivation names its `:stage`).  The text never includes a host\n   172\t   exception message, so it is identical on every host and VM.\"\n   173\t  [indexer]\n   174\t  (let [{:keys [reason stage]} (:failure indexer)]\n   175\t    (cond\n   176\t      (:lost? indexer)\n   177\t      (str \"Warning: the AST index lost a program batch;\"\n   178\t           \" $ast and $occ are unavailable until (reset)\")\n   179\t\n   180\t      (:failure indexer)\n   181\t      (str \"Warning: the AST index refused a program (\"\n   182\t           (name (or reason stage))\n   183\t           \"); $ast and $occ are unavailable until (reset)\"))))\n   184\t\n   185\t\n   186\t(defn status\n   187\t  \"The AST indexer's state as the shell reports it.  It depends only on the\n   188\t   expanded programs, never on which evaluator ran them, so every VM\n   189\t   reports the same status for the same inputs.\"\n   190\t  [indexer]\n   191\t  {:programs (:programs indexer)\n   192\t   :rows (count (:rows indexer))\n   193\t   :occurrences (count (:occurrences indexer))\n   194\t   :lost? (:lost? indexer)\n   195\t   :gaps (:ingress-gaps (:observer indexer) 0)\n   196\t   :failure (:failure indexer)})\n   225\t\n   226\t(defn- index-packets\n   227\t  \"Step a fresh AST indexer over `packets` on a medium of its own.\"\n   228\t  [packets]\n   229\t  (let [{:keys [writer observer]} (small-medium 16)]\n   230\t    (doseq [p packets] (stream/append! writer p))\n   231\t    (ast-index/step (ast-index/make-indexer {:observer observer}))))\n   232\t\n   233\t\n   234\t(deftest a-malformed-packet-leaves-the-relations-unavailable\n   235\t  (let [[root rows] (literal-packet 1)\n   236\t        good (literal-packet 2)]\n   237\t    (doseq [[label packet reason]\n   238\t            [[\"not a packet\" \"garbage\" :shape]\n   239\t             [\"rows not rows\" [root [:x]] :shape]\n   240\t             [\"an unknown tag\" [root [[root :no-such-tag]]] :invalid-rows]\n   241\t             [\"a missing root\" [root []] :invalid-rows]\n   242\t             [\"one address, two rows\"\n   243\t              [root (conj rows (assoc (first rows) 2 :other))]\n   244\t              :duplicate-address]\n   245\t             [\"one address, the same row twice\"\n   246\t              [root (conj rows (first rows))]\n   247\t              :duplicate-address]\n   248\t             [\"a well-formed row under a forged address\"\n   249\t              (let [forged (first (literal-packet 3))]\n   250\t                [forged [(assoc (first rows) 0 forged)]])\n   251\t              :address-mismatch]]]\n   252\t      (testing label\n   253\t        (let [ix (index-packets [good packet good])]\n   254\t          (is (= reason (get-in ix [:failure :reason])))\n   255\t          (is (nil? (ast-index/relations ix)) \"never a partial snapshot\")\n   256\t          (is (= 1 (:programs (ast-index/status ix)))\n   257\t              \"the packet before it was indexed, none after\")\n   258\t          (is (false? (:lost? (ast-index/status ix)))))))\n   259\t    (testing \"a row forged under an address already held\"\n   260\t      (let [[groot grows] good\n   261\t            forged [groot (mapv #(if (= groot (first %)) (assoc % 2 99) %)\n   262\t                                grows)]\n   263\t            ix (index-packets [good forged])]\n   264\t        (is (= :address-mismatch (get-in ix [:failure :reason])))\n   265\t        (is (nil? (ast-index/relations ix)))))\n   266\t    (testing \"an address already holding a metadata-distinct row\"\n   267\t      ;; yin.vm.macro-test's fixture: the canonical encoding strips reader\n   268\t      ;; positions, so bodies differing only there share one address\n   269\t      (let [literal-row (fn [v]\n   270\t                          (let [body [:literal v]]\n   271\t                            (into [(jing/segment-key body)] body)))\n   272\t            r1 (literal-row (with-meta 'x {:line 1}))\n   273\t            r2 (literal-row (with-meta 'x {:line 2}))\n   274\t            ix (index-packets [[(first r1) [r1]] [(first r2) [r2]]])]\n   275\t        (is (= (first r1) (first r2)) \"the address strips reader positions\")\n   276\t        (is (= :address-conflict (get-in ix [:failure :reason])))\n   277\t        (is (= (first r2) (get-in ix [:failure :id])))\n   278\t        (is (nil? (ast-index/relations ix)))\n   279\t        (is (= {:line 1} (meta (nth (get-in ix [:rows (first r1)]) 2)))\n   280\t            \"the held row is not replaced\")\n   281\t        (is (nil? (:failure (index-packets [[(first r1) [r1]]\n   282\t                                            [(first r1) [r1]]])))\n   283\t            \"an identical row observed again merges\")\n   284\t        (is (= :duplicate-address\n   285\t               (get-in (index-packets [[(first r1) [r1 r2]]]) [:failure :reason]))\n   286\t            \"within one packet, the metadata-distinct pair is refused too\")\n   287\t        (testing \"a difference nested inside metadata\"\n   288\t          (let [n1 (literal-row (with-meta 'x {:doc (with-meta 'd {:line 1})}))\n   289\t                n2 (literal-row (with-meta 'x {:doc (with-meta 'd {:line 2})}))]\n   290\t            (is (= (first n1) (first n2)))\n   291\t            (is (= :address-conflict\n   292\t                   (get-in (index-packets [[(first n1) [n1]] [(first n2) [n2]]])\n   293\t                           [:failure :reason])))))))\n   294\t    (testing \"a well-formed stream stays available\"\n   295\t      (let [ix (index-packets [good (literal-packet 1) good])]\n   296\t        (is (nil? (:failure ix)))\n   297\t        (is (= 2 (count (:ast (ast-index/relations ix)))))\n   298\t        (is (= 3 (:programs (ast-index/status ix))))))))\n   299\t\n   300\t\n   301\t(deftest a-malformed-packet-in-the-session-is-reported-and-evaluation-continues\n   302\t  (let [{:keys [writer observer]} (small-medium 4)\n   303\t        _ (stream/append! writer \"garbage\")\n   304\t        state (assoc-in (repl/create-state) [:ast-indexer :observer] observer)\n   305\t        [state' text] (repl/eval-input state \"(+ 1 2)\")\n   306\t        [state'' text'] (repl/eval-input state' \"(+ 2 3)\")\n   307\t        [_ result] (repl/eval-input (first (repl/eval-input state'' \"(reset)\"))\n   308\t                                    \"(+ 1 2)\")]\n   309\t    (is (= (str \"3\\n\" (refused-warning \"shape\")) text))\n   310\t    (is (= (str \"5\\n\" (refused-warning \"shape\")) text')\n   311\t        \"every round warns until (reset)\")\n   312\t    (is (= \"3\" result))\n   313\t    (is (= :shape (get-in (repl/repl-state state') [:ast-index :failure :reason])))\n   314\t    (is (nil? (relations state')))))\n   315\t\n   316\t\n   317\t(deftest a-refused-packet-names-its-cause-in-the-warning\n   318\t  (let [{:keys [writer observer]} (small-medium 4)\n   319\t        [root rows] (literal-packet 1)\n   320\t        _ (stream/append! writer [root (conj rows (first rows))])\n   321\t        state (assoc-in (repl/create-state) [:ast-indexer :observer] observer)\n   322\t        [_ text] (repl/eval-input state \"(+ 1 2)\")]\n   323\t    (is (= (str \"3\\n\" (refused-warning \"duplicate-address\")) text))))\n   324\t\n   325\t\n   326\t(deftest healthy-rounds-carry-no-warning-on-every-vm\n   327\t  (doseq [vm-type (keys repl/vm-constructors)]\n   328\t    (let [[_ texts] (evaluate (repl/create-state {:vm-type vm-type})\n   329\t                              [\"(+ 1 2)\" \"(+ 2 3)\"])]\n   330\t      (is (= [\"3\" \"5\"] texts) (str vm-type)))))\n   331\t\n   332\t\n   333\t(deftest the-lost-warning-is-identical-on-every-vm\n   334\t  (doseq [vm-type (keys repl/vm-constructors)]\n   335\t    (let [{:keys [writer observer]} (small-medium 1)\n   336\t          _ (doseq [v [1 2]] (stream/append! writer (literal-packet v)))\n   337\t          state (assoc-in (repl/create-state {:vm-type vm-type})\n   338\t                          [:ast-indexer :observer] observer)\n   339\t          [_ text] (repl/eval-input state \"(+ 1 2)\")]\n   340\t      (is (= (str \"3\\n\" lost-warning) text) (str vm-type)))))\n   341\t\n   342\t\n   343\t(deftest both-indexers-unhealthy-warn-code-index-first\n   344\t  (let [code (small-medium 1)\n   345\t        ast (small-medium 1)\n   346\t        _ (doseq [m [code ast]\n   347\t                  v [1 2]]\n   348\t            (stream/append! (:writer m) (literal-packet v)))\n   349\t        state (-> (repl/create-state)\n   350\t                  (assoc-in [:indexer :observer] (:observer code))\n   351\t                  (assoc-in [:ast-indexer :observer] (:observer ast)))\n   352\t        [_ text] (repl/eval-input state \"(+ 1 2)\")\n   353\t        [head code-warning ast-warning & more] (str/split-lines text)]\n   354\t    (is (= \"3\" head))\n   355\t    (is (str/starts-with? code-warning \"Warning: the code index lost\"))\ndiff --git a/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc b/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc\nindex 5c3db835..2f3cdd7c 100644\n--- a/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc\n+++ b/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc\n@@ -19,6 +19,7 @@\n             [yang.clojure :as yang.clojure]\n             [yang.php :as yang.php]\n             [yang.python :as yang.python]\n+            [yin.repl.ast-index :as ast-index]\n             [yin.repl.index :as index]\n             [yin.repl.link :as link]\n             [yin.repl.query :as query]\n@@ -721,7 +722,9 @@\n    which loads each packet and runs it.  The code indexer's observer\n    (`yin.repl.index`) is a peer attached to `program-out` beside it; the\n    round advances each, and neither calls the other.  It records\n-   `shell-token` as provenance and publishes into `index-store`.\n+   `shell-token` as provenance and publishes into `index-store`.  The AST\n+   indexer (`yin.repl.ast-index`), holding the session's `$ast` and `$occ`\n+   relations, is a third such peer.\n \n    The link pair is the session's (`yin.repl.link/make-pair`): the VM's\n    half lives in its private `:resources`, the interpreter's half beside\n@@ -750,6 +753,7 @@\n      :indexer (index/make-indexer {:observer ((:attach program-out))\n                                    :session-token shell-token\n                                    :content-store index-store})\n+     :ast-indexer (ast-index/make-indexer {:observer ((:attach program-out))})\n      :link-pair pair\n      :query-pair (dissoc query-pair :out-cursor)}))\n \n@@ -981,7 +985,8 @@\n                        :observer (drain-observer (resume (:observer state)))\n                        :row-observer (drain-observer\n                                        (resume (:row-observer state)))\n-                       :indexer (index/skip (:indexer state)))\n+                       :indexer (index/skip (:indexer state))\n+                       :ast-indexer (ast-index/skip (:ast-indexer state)))\n         [state' output-text]\n         (drain-output\n           (cond-> drained\n@@ -999,11 +1004,21 @@\n   (update state :indexer index/step (:round state)))\n \n \n+(defn- run-ast-index-stage\n+  \"Drive the AST indexer's observer over `program-out`: it adds each\n+   forwarded packet's rows and occurrences to the session's `$ast` and\n+   `$occ` relations.  It runs before the evaluator for the same reason the\n+   code indexer does, and neither indexer reads the other.\"\n+  [state]\n+  (update state :ast-indexer ast-index/step))\n+\n+\n (defn- with-index-notice\n-  \"Append what the round's index step lost, if anything, to its result\n-   text; the evaluation's own answer is unchanged.\"\n-  [[state text] notice]\n-  (if notice\n+  \"Append what the round's index steps lost, if anything, to its result\n+   text, one line per notice in the order given; the evaluation's own\n+   answer is unchanged.\"\n+  [[state text] notices]\n+  (if-let [notice (some->> (remove nil? notices) seq (str/join \"\\n\"))]\n     [state (if (str/blank? text) notice (str text \"\\n\" notice))]\n     [state text]))\n \n@@ -1381,7 +1396,7 @@ Hint: If you wanted to evaluate these datoms as data, use a quote: '[[...]]\"\n    datom-literal program — through the §10.1 composition.  The encoder\n    projects it to an input batch of canonical rows with its harvest and\n    declaration rows; the shell appends that batch to `program-in`, drives\n-   the expander, drains its summary, and drives the code indexer and then\n+   the expander, drains its summary, and drives the code and AST indexers and then\n    the evaluator only when a program was forwarded.  An expansion failure is reported as data: its\n    batch is consumed, the store keeps its previous macros, and the next\n    input evaluates normally.  An encoding failure throws before anything\n@@ -1415,7 +1430,8 @@ Hint: If you wanted to evaluate these datoms as data, use a quote: '[[...]]\"\n             failed\n             (let [[expanded {:keys [errors forwarded]}] expanded\n                   